# Code Quality Rules

## Comments

- Default: NO comments
- Add only when WHY is non-obvious
- Never explain what the code does

## Modules

- ES Modules only: `import`/`export`
- `require()` and `module.exports` PROHIBITED
- Explicit `.js` extension on all relative imports

## Async

- `async/await` only
- `try/catch` in every async function
- No `.then()` / `.catch()` chains (except fire-and-forget emails)

## Variables

- `const` default, `let` when reassigned, never `var`
- Models: PascalCase
- Controllers/utils/services: camelCase
- Components: PascalCase
- Hooks: `useX`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`

## Forbidden

- `require()` / `module.exports`
- `var`
- Anonymous default exports
- Nested ternaries
- `console.log` in production code
- `process.exit()` in handlers

## Style

- Early returns over nesting
- One responsibility per function
- No abstractions beyond what the task requires
